# Client Project Workflow — The Agency

You are executing The Agency's repeatable client project workflow. This skill guides you through building professional landing pages and websites for clients.

## Workflow Phases

Follow these phases in order for each client project:

### Phase 1: Client Intake
**Goal:** Gather all information before starting

**Checklist:**
- [ ] Client name & company
- [ ] Project deadline
- [ ] Budget & payment terms
- [ ] Domain (do they have one?)
- [ ] Brand assets (logo, colors, messaging)
- [ ] Website content (copy, images, videos)
- [ ] Target audience
- [ ] Main goal (convert leads, show portfolio, drive sales)

**Key Questions to Ask:**
- "What's your main conversion goal?"
- "Do you have a domain, or should we buy one?"
- "Is content ready, or do you need help with copy?"
- "Timeline - when do you need this live?"

**Pricing Options:**
- One-time fee: $2,500-5,000
- With monthly support: $2,500 + $150-300/mo
- Monthly retainer (you own domain): $49-99/mo

---

### Phase 2: Project Setup
**Goal:** Create GitHub repo, Vercel project, and configure domain

**Step 1: Create GitHub Repository**
```bash
# Clone the template
git clone https://github.com/neutronix007/sharpe-designed-it.git [client-name]-landing
cd [client-name]-landing

# Update repo info
# Edit package.json - change name to: client-name-landing

# Create new GitHub repo at github.com/new
# Make it PRIVATE

# Update remote and push
git remote set-url origin https://github.com/yourusername/[client-name]-landing.git
git push -u origin main
```

**Step 2: Create Vercel Project**
1. Go to vercel.com/new
2. Import GitHub repo
3. Framework: Vite (auto-detected)
4. Deploy

**Step 3: Configure Domain**

**If client has domain (recommended):**
- [ ] Get domain registrar info from client
- [ ] Add CNAME record:
  - Name: `@` (or `www`)
  - Value: `cname.vercel-dns.com`
- [ ] Add domain to Vercel (Settings → Domains)
- [ ] Wait 15-30 mins for SSL certificate

**If you buy domain:**
- [ ] Buy on Namecheap (~$12/year)
- [ ] Point to Vercel (CNAME or nameservers)
- [ ] Add to Vercel project
- [ ] Invoice client $12 or add to monthly fee

---

### Phase 3: Development
**Goal:** Customize template with client branding and content

**Files to Update:**
- `src/components/Hero.tsx` - Main headline/CTA
- `src/components/Features.tsx` - Services/features section
- `src/index.css` - Brand colors
- `src/components/ContactForm.tsx` - Update Formspree ID
- `public/` - Add client logo, images, videos
- `src/App.tsx` - Update page title/meta

**Customization Checklist:**
- [ ] Update colors (primary, secondary, accent)
- [ ] Update all copy (headlines, descriptions)
- [ ] Add client images/videos to public/
- [ ] Update logo
- [ ] Update contact form email/Formspree ID
- [ ] Update SEO title, description, og:image
- [ ] Remove unused sections
- [ ] Test on mobile

**Development Workflow:**
```bash
# Run dev server
npm run dev

# Make changes, test locally
# Commit regularly
git add .
git commit -m "Update [section] for [client]"

# Push to GitHub
git push origin main

# ✅ Vercel auto-deploys!
```

---

### Phase 4: Testing & Launch
**Goal:** Verify everything works before handing off

**Pre-Launch Checklist:**
- [ ] Domain resolves correctly (no SSL warnings)
- [ ] Green lock icon (SSL active)
- [ ] All text is final (no typos)
- [ ] Images load correctly
- [ ] All buttons/links work
- [ ] Contact form submits successfully
- [ ] Page loads in <3 seconds
- [ ] Mobile responsive (tested on phone)

**Test Contact Form:**
1. Fill out form on live site
2. Submit
3. Verify email arrives in inbox
4. Reply to confirm it works

---

### Phase 5: Handoff
**Goal:** Deliver to client and collect payment

**Create Handoff Document:**
```
Your Site is Live! 🎉

📍 Live URL: [their-domain.com]
📧 Contact form emails go to: [their email]
🔐 Vercel handles security & updates automatically

What to do next:
1. Test the contact form
2. Share with team/investors
3. Drive traffic to it
4. Contact me with any changes

Support: [your contact info]
```

**Complete Handoff:**
- [ ] Handoff document sent
- [ ] Invoice paid
- [ ] Domain control transferred (if applicable)
- [ ] GitHub access given (if they want code access)
- [ ] Support plan confirmed

---

### Phase 6: Maintenance (Optional)
**Goal:** Provide ongoing support and collect recurring revenue

**Monthly Tasks:**
- [ ] Check site loads correctly
- [ ] Respond to contact form messages
- [ ] Monitor performance (Vercel analytics)

**Support Packages:**
- **Basic ($50/mo):** Email support, small tweaks
- **Standard ($150/mo):** Monthly updates, analytics reviews
- **Premium ($300/mo):** Weekly check-ins, new features, full support

---

## Quick Reference

### Commands Cheat Sheet
```bash
# Clone template
git clone https://github.com/neutronix007/sharpe-designed-it.git [name]-landing

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Run dev server
npm run dev

# Push changes
git add .
git commit -m "Update [what changed]"
git push origin main
```

### Files to Always Update
1. `src/components/Hero.tsx` - Headline, CTA
2. `src/index.css` - Colors
3. `public/` - Logo, images
4. `src/App.tsx` - SEO title

### Cost Breakdown Per Client
| Item | Cost | Notes |
|------|------|-------|
| Domain | $12/year | If you buy |
| Vercel | FREE | No cost |
| GitHub | FREE | No cost |
| Your work | $2,500-5,000 | Main revenue |
| Support | $50-300/mo | Optional recurring |

---

## Common Issues & Fixes

| Problem | Solution |
|---------|----------|
| "Not secure" warning | Wait 30 mins for SSL, check DNS |
| Contact form not working | Verify Formspree ID in code |
| Images don't load | Check path in public/ folder |
| Site slow | Optimize images, check Vercel |
| Client wants changes | Update code, push to GitHub, auto-deploys |

---

## Key Principles

✅ **What Works:**
- Separate Vercel project per client
- Path-based routing (no subdomain complexity)
- Formspree for contact forms
- Client owns domain OR you charge monthly

❌ **What Doesn't:**
- Shared subdomains on one app
- Manual DNS management
- Traditional hosting (cPanel)

